.An Dick Olsson Aq Mt hi@senzilla.io
.Sh SECURITY CONSIDERATIONS
.Nm
generates a random root password for each installation and stores it
in the VM state directory.
When the installed image goes into the cache,
.Nm
also stores the password in the
.Pa meta.json
of that entry
.Pq mode 0600 .
The cache makes the life of this secret longer:
the password stays after
.Cm destroy ,
and it changes only when the base key changes.
.Pp
The guest permits password root login.
.Cm put
and
.Cm get
reach the guest as root,
over the forwarded SSH port.
The console port carries no authentication of its own,
and the guest login prompt is the only gate.
.Nm
binds the forwarded SSH port and the telnet serial console to
.Ar bind_address ,
and the default is
.Li 127.0.0.1 .
Thus only the host itself reaches a guest.
.Ar bind_address 0.0.0.0
makes both ports listen on each host interface.
Treat such a VM as open to all persons who can reach the host.
The password is then not a localhost-only secret.
Apply the same rule to a
.Ar cache_dir
that has content.
.Pp
An
.Xr autoinstall 8
response file can hold the root password of the guest.
The responder of the autoinstall mode binds
.Li 127.0.0.1
only,
and the guest reaches it through the QEMU gateway,
so no other machine can fetch the file.
.Nm
never copies the file into the cache or into the state directory,
and the image-cache key holds a digest of the file,
not its content.
The first line of
.Ar root_password_file
is a secret of the same kind:
.Nm
reads the file where it needs the value,
and it warns when the file mode lets the group or another user read
it.
.Pp
The host verifies each mirror download under the release key,
with
.Xr signify 1 ,
before the file enters the cache,
and a file that fails leaves no copy behind.
The guest installer verifies its own sets under the key in
.Pa bsd.rd ,
.Xr pkg_add 1
verifies each package,
and a distfile verifies against the
.Pa distinfo
digest of the verified ports tree,
in the guest.
The shipped key under
.Pa share/fuguvm/signify/
is a trust anchor:
a human adds each key file,
and the commit that adds one states the comparison against
.Pa /etc/signify/
on a real
.Ox
host of that release.
.Ar verify no
removes the host proof and the installer proof together;
use it only against a mirror that something else verifies.
